    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>of Computer Science Unit Foundation Concepts The unit focuses on Algorithmic Classification and Pattern Discovery. It explores the mechanics of Supervised Learning (predicting labels) and Unsupervised Learning (discovering structure). Key themes include Proximity-based Logic, Entropy-driven Decisions, and Optimization through parameter refinement.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.3.4</strong> — Supervised Learning Models: K-Nearest Neighbours (K-NN) (distance metrics) and Decision Trees (splitting criteria).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.3.5</strong> — Model Optimization: Hyperparameter tuning (k-value in K-NN, depth in trees) to balance bias and variance.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.3.6</strong> — Unsupervised Learning: Clustering (grouping similar data points without labels).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A4.3.7</strong> — Association Rule Mining: Discovering relationships between variables (e.g., Market Basket Analysis).
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

